Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimePedestrianCrossing" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasEvidence :indicator1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :night1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 ;
    :occursInScene :scene1 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "A child running into the street" .

:indicator1 a :RollingBallIndicator ;
    :description "A ball rolling into the road indicates potential child pedestrian activity" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:night1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "High risk of collision with a pedestrian entering the vehicle path at night" ;
    :confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.95"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Potential collision with a pedestrian (child) who has entered the roadway unexpectedly, preceded by the rolling ball evidence indicator.
Severity Score: 0.95